Advocacy and coverage of needle exchange programs: Results of a comparative study of harm reduction programs in Brazil, Bangladesh, Belarus, Ukraine, Russian Federation, and China</article-title><source>Cad Saude Publica</source><year>2006</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>871</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16612440</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rose</surname><given-names>VJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Raymond</surname><given-names>HF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kellogg</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>McFarland</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessing the feasibility of harm reduction services for MSM: The late night breakfast buffet study</article-title><source>Harm Reduction Journal</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>29</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17018154</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1477-7517-3-29</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allott</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Redman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patterns of use and harm reduction practices of ecstasy users in Australia</article-title><source>Drug Alcohol Depend</source><year>2006</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>168</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16226850</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.drugalcdep.2005.09.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Savitz</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanzer</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mirvish</surname><given-names>SS</given-names><